{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<ol><li>Pin versions in <code>importmap.json</code>.</li><li>Vendor the packages with <code>importmap vendor</code>, for example through <code>go generate</code>, and commit the files and the lock.</li><li>Check them in CI with <code>importmap verify</code>, which needs no network.</li><li>Embed the directory and load it with <code>FromFS</code>.</li><li>Serve the files with <code>ServeFile</code>; nothing is fetched during page requests.</li></ol>
<pre><code># when a pin changes
go generate ./...

# in CI
go run github.com/donseba/go-importmap/cmd/importmap verify -out assets/vendor
go build ./...</code></pre>
<p><a href="{{ basePath }}/vendoring" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/vendoring" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">Vendoring</a> describes the configuration, the flags and the lock file. <code>-timeout</code> bounds the downloads of <code>importmap vendor</code>; the default is <code>2m</code>.</p>
<h2>Offline serving</h2>
<p>With <code>FromFS</code> the binary holds every file, and the lock is checked when the import map is built, so a missing or changed file fails at start-up rather than in the browser. The provider and the package cache belong to the build; they need not be present in the deployed runtime. No module shim is loaded unless <code>ShimPath</code> sets one; a remote shim URL, <code>Raw</code> imports and remote imports inside module files still reach other hosts.</p>
<h2>Reproducibility and updates</h2>
<p>The configuration pins versions and the lock records each file's source and SHA-384 integrity, so a diff of the lock shows what an update changed. Change a pin, vendor again, and commit the result. URLs carry each file's version (<code>?v=…</code>), so browsers may cache a file for a year and still receive the new one after a deploy.</p>
<h2>Fetching at start-up</h2>
<pre><code>ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), time.Minute)
defer cancel()
im.WithLogger(slog.Default())
if err := im.CacheOrFetch(ctx); err != nil { return err }</code></pre>
<p>Without vendoring, the application prepares its assets at start-up. A timeout bounds metadata requests and downloads. Without the <code>.importmap</code> cache, start-up needs the network. Return preparation failures to the start-up command; do not continue serving a newly prepared version after a failed preparation step. Fingerprint the published files with <code>assets.Fingerprint</code> and pass the manifest to <code>WithAssets</code> to get versioned URLs on this path too.</p>
</article>
